                        "entry_id": "49cd1b32-7b94-3697-a325-48d6dd10e46b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That which sails; a sailboat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab81df96-471d-4ba4-b6dc-05fc2a3bab97",
                                "sense_id": "1dbd1771-17bd-3146-a80d-7e768b9832df",
                                "text": "She is the best sailer in the service, and she carries a hundred guns."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a954a3fc-8e34-438d-a213-f2ea7ffc1181",
                                "sense_id": "1dbd1771-17bd-3146-a80d-7e768b9832df",
                                "text": "The Gulnare was a fast sailer, built for a slaver originally[.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7d2b1ef-404c-44f0-8360-93661237a6de",
                                "sense_id": "1dbd1771-17bd-3146-a80d-7e768b9832df",
                                "text": "Elsewhere it has been said that in the lack of frigates (of course better sailers than line-of-battle ships) in the English squadron up the Straits at that period, the Indomitable was occasionally employed not only as an available substitute for a scout, but at times on detached service of more important kind."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
